// Per-product panel configuration. This carries the cross-cutting, deep-in-the-tree product knobs that
// apps can't easily prop-drill (brand name + wording/badge toggles consumed by PanelHeader, PanelTabs,
// ProfilePane, ApplyStatus, etc. — components that live inside PanelCard's subtree). Each product's
// panel entry wraps its tree in <PanelConfigProvider value={...}>; everything not supplied falls back to
// these defaults, which reproduce the BidHub Copilot UI exactly (so apps that provide nothing are
// unchanged, and the context works even with no provider).
//
//   brandName         — product name shown in the panel (header, welcome, update/banner copy)
//   profileMode       — 'multi' (selectable profiles, "the selected profile" wording) or
//                        'single' (one auto-bound profile, "your profile" wording, no "not selected")
//   showProfileSharing— show the ownership (Owned/Shared) badge + access-level row in ProfilePane
//   showMonitoringUI  — show screen-monitoring UI (header notice + ProfilePane screenshot row)
//   paymentMode       — 'credits' (BidHub pay-as-you-go: per-action price, "insufficient credit",
//                        top-up balance) or 'subscription' (AmboHire: plan/entitlement, "upgrade"
//                        instead of credit wording, no per-action price)
//   openProfilesLabel — label/tooltip for the header globe button ('Open profiles' for BidHub's
//                        multi-profile app, 'Open Profile' for AmboHire's single-profile app)
//   openProfilesPage  — the `page` key the button sends in the openPage message; the background
//                        handler (background/ui.js) maps it to the product's real profile URL
//   openApplyAgentPage— the `page` key the Job pane's Apply Agent lane sends in the openPage
//                        message for the product's Apply Agent page ('applyAgent' = BidHub's
//                        per-profile /profiles/:id/apply-agent, 'autoApply' = AmboHire's flat
//                        /auto-apply); background/ui.js maps it and appends the allow-listed status
//                        query the lane passes along
